<footer class="mt-auto bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 border-slate-200 border-t dark:border-slate-700">
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-start justify-between md:flex-row md:items-center">
      <div class="flex gap-2 items-center">
        <span class="relative inline-block h-5 w-5 shrink-0 rounded-full border-2 border-emerald-500" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="absolute -top-0.5 left-1/2 h-1.5 w-1.5 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="font-semibold gradient-text">WildLoop</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm dark:text-slate-400">
        Find trails. Track miles. Hold ground.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!--
      Data attribution. Not decoration: OpenStreetMap is published under the
      ODbL, which requires that any product built on it credits the source and
      names the licence. The two federal datasets are public domain and need no
      permission, but saying where a trail came from is what lets someone judge
      whether to trust it.
    -->
    <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700">
      <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        Trail data from
        <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-slate-300 dark:decoration-slate-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-600 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 transition">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>
        (<a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/" rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-slate-300 dark:decoration-slate-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-600 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 transition">ODbL</a>),
        the <a href="https://data.fs.usda.gov/geodata/edw/datasets.php" rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-slate-300 dark:decoration-slate-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-600 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 transition">USDA Forest Service</a>
        and the <a href="https://public-nps.opendata.arcgis.com/" rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-slate-300 dark:decoration-slate-600 underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-600 dark:hover:text-emerald-400 transition">National Park Service</a>.
        Conditions change. Check with the land manager before you go.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
